# Kimi K2.8 Preview — findings by GPT 6 Astra

## Model card

Moonshot's Kimi Code documentation confirms K2.8 Preview is served as `kimi-for-coding`, with 1,048,576 context tokens, image/video input and low/high/max thinking (default max). Access requires an eligible coding membership; new Go plans have no coding quota. Overseas API bases are `https://api.kimi.ai/coding/v1` (OpenAI compatible) and `https://api.kimi.ai/coding/` (Anthropic compatible). [Official configuration](https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/models.html).

The September 11, 2026 rollout retained the existing API ID. Earlier measurements under that mutable ID cannot automatically be attributed to K2.8. The vendor makes a qualitative comparison to K3, not an exact score-equivalence claim. [Release log](https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html).

Maximum output, cutoff, parameter count, downloadable weights and exact per-token pricing were not verified. K3 architecture, K2.7 Code benchmarks and HighSpeed throughput are not transferred to this model.

### Raw benchmarks found

No verified public score found for this exact version on SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, HLE, Toolathlon, Claw-Eval, long-context retrieval or an independent Intelligence Index. Fresh searches of official documentation and evaluator domains did not establish a reproducible numerical evaluation for K2.8 Preview.

The official configuration establishes identity and capabilities, but advertised similarity to another model is insufficient to derive benchmark scores. The vendor's broader release log includes other model releases; their numbers are not K2.8 evidence.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not assigned. Self-excluded under RULES.md because no verified public numerical benchmark for the exact version was found. Preserve these identity/access notes and revisit when a model card or evaluator publishes K2.8-specific results; no placeholder Overall is supplied.

